-- @nonassertable marks a named step; above anything else it is a check error
-- naming what it sits on (specs/todo/presumption-assertion/CONTRACT.md §6).
-- Errors expected, one each: the DECLARE, the ASSUME, the section heading, the
-- directive, and a mark on a definition's GIVEN line, which names the input.
-- The marks above the two definitions are fine.

@nonassertable
DECLARE Person HAS name IS A STRING

@nonassertable
ASSUME `is adult` IS A BOOLEAN

@nonassertable
`can vote` MEANS `is adult`

@nonassertable
§ `Part Two`
    GIVEN `is resident` IS A BOOLEAN

@nonassertable
`can stand` MEANS `is resident`

@nonassertable
#EVAL `can vote`

GIVEN x IS A BOOLEAN @nonassertable
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`signature marked` MEANS x
